{
  "description": "Shared AnnouncementSpeechBuilder vectors. Loaded by the Kotlin and Swift tests. 'config' uses the field names of AnnouncementStateData; templates are literal here so only the structured parts are checked (rounding, units, clock format, decimal separator, label fallbacks), not translated wording. A case with 'preview': true runs buildPreview(config); otherwise build(config, distanceMeters, elapsedSeconds) with the lastAnnouncement* fields applied to the config. Decimals round the value's shortest decimal form with ties to even (Foundation's %.1f behaviour), so 1.25 is '1.2', 0.15 is '0.2' and 1.75 is '1.8'; Java's String.format rounds half up instead and was replaced in the Kotlin builder.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "one kilometre in five minutes",
      "config": {
        "enabled": true,
        "intervalUnit": "distance",
        "distanceIntervalMeters": 1000.0,
        "timeIntervalSeconds": 300,
        "useImperialUnits": false,
        "metric": "pace",
        "languageTag": "en-US",
        "distanceUnitTemplate": "{value} km",
        "metricUnitTemplate": "{value} min/km",
        "metricLabel": "Pace",
        "messageTemplate": "D[{distance}] T[{duration}] L[{lapMetric}] O[{overallMetric}]"
      },
      "distanceMeters": 1000.0,
      "elapsedSeconds": 300,
      "lastAnnouncementDistanceMeters": 0.0,
      "lastAnnouncementElapsedSeconds": 0,
      "expect": "D[1.0 km] T[5:00] L[Pace 5:00 min/km] O[Pace 5:00 min/km]"
